# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out as LF everywhere, Windows
# included. `text=auto` alone would not do that: with `core.autocrlf=true` set globally - which is the
# default on Windows installs - every checkout would rewrite these files to CRLF, and the result is
# whole-file diffs that depend on whose machine committed rather than on what changed.
#
# `eol=lf` is the right side of that choice for this repository specifically: Prettier, the Angular
# CLI and every Node tool here emit LF, and there is no Windows batch script in the tree that needs
# CRLF to run. (The backend repository marks `*.cmd` as `eol=crlf` for exactly that reason; nothing
# here is in that position.)
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so Git neither diffs them nor touches their bytes looking for line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated and enormous. Still committed - it is what makes an install reproducible - but excluded
# from diffs and from language statistics so it stops drowning every review it appears in.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
